load ../credential-region-escape.maude

--- Fixture shape. Region r1 is open with v1 (secret) bound inside it.
--- `closeReq(r1)` is always present, so every search explores both the branch
--- where in-region work happens first and the branch where the region closes
--- first.

--- Coverage: derivation inside an open region works and the derived value
--- inherits the region. The mechanism does something.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) deriveReq(v1, v2)
  =>* C:Cfg inRegion(v2, secret, r1) .

--- Coverage: EXIT 1 end to end. A granted declassify inside the region
--- produces ordinary held data that outlives the close and reaches the durable
--- fact base. Without this the escape theorems would hold on a region that
--- produces nothing, which is not the design being checked.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) grantDeclassify
  declassifyReq(v1) sinkReq(v1)
  =>* C:Cfg regionClosed(r1) persistedPlain(v1, public) .

--- Coverage: EXIT 2 end to end. A value derived inside the region is re-sealed
--- and the ciphertext outlives the close.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) custody
  deriveReq(v1, v2) resealReq(v2)
  =>* C:Cfg regionClosed(r1) sealedVal(v2, secret) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture. `open` marks rather than binds, so the value
--- survives the close as ordinary held data at its SEALED label. Note that
--- DR-0074 §4 has not been violated anywhere inside the region -- every
--- crossing there obeyed it; the violation is entirely after the closing brace.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE-ESCAPING :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1)
  =>* C:Cfg regionClosed(r1) holds(v1, secret) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture, the consequence that matters. Escape re-enables
--- a §4 violation through a route the materialization model cannot see: the
--- value is persisted at its sealed label, having become ordinary data first.
--- This is why §3.1 is load-bearing rather than hygiene.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE-ESCAPING :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) sinkReq(v1)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedPlain(v1, secret) .

--- THEOREM E1. No in-region value ever becomes ordinary held data at its
--- sealed label, however the close interleaves with the in-region work. Both
--- exits are present and live in this fixture, so the region is not a dead end
--- and the No-solution has content. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) grantDeclassify custody
  declassifyReq(v1) resealReq(v1) deriveReq(v1, v2)
  =>* holds(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM E1, on a DERIVED value. A projection computed inside the region
--- escapes no more easily than the value it came from. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) grantDeclassify custody
  deriveReq(v1, v2) declassifyReq(v2) resealReq(v2)
  =>* holds(v2, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM E2, the tie-back. Escape never re-enables persistence at the sealed
--- label. The materialization model's C1 covers crossings made from INSIDE the
--- region; this covers the route that leaves the region first and persists
--- afterwards, which C1 cannot see. Together they close both. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionOpen(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) closeReq(r1) grantDeclassify custody
  declassifyReq(v1) resealReq(v1) sinkReq(v1)
  =>* persistedPlain(v1, secret) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: the exits are REGION-SCOPED, not merely granted. Presented with a
--- region that has already closed, a fully granted declassify does nothing --
--- so `close` is a real boundary rather than a bookkeeping marker, and the
--- coverage searches above pass because their exits ran while open.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-ESCAPE :
  regionClosed(r1) inRegion(v1, secret, r1) grantDeclassify custody
  declassifyReq(v1) resealReq(v1)
  =>* holds(v1, public) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
